  "findings": [
    {
      "lemma": "2.1",
      "status": "PASS",
      "scope": "Balanced separation is correct when all weights are nonnegative and at least one positive weight has a nonzero direction. The three-vector identity itself does not enforce positivity."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "2.2",
      "status": "PASS_WITH_ROTATION_CONVENTION",
      "scope": "All four reduction moves and the Euler form hold for a finite proper rotation group. Ry(phi) uses [[cos,0,-sin],[0,1,0],[sin,0,cos]] to match the paper's X(theta,phi). The opposite active-rotation convention negates the horizontal components of X. Common proper N realizes simultaneous view negation."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "3.1",
      "status": "PASS_WITH_RANGE_REQUIREMENT",
      "scope": "Rodrigues expression and error coefficient norm verified exactly. The min-over-maximizers step uses sin(s)>0 and finite tan(s/2), thus requires the local range 0<s<pi."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "5.1",
      "status": "PASS",
      "scope": "Verified with all nine entries of the basis matrix symbolic. Common division preserves balance where the factor is nonzero; exact polynomial quotients extend the identity to the zero set."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "5.2",
      "status": "LOGICAL_GAP",
      "scope": "Common sign does not imply nonnegative weights. The criterion with common negative weights can accept a strict passage. The rectangular-box example refutes that generic criterion, not the snub-specific no-Rupert conclusion or the actual certificate data."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "4.3 W plane",
